1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:13,804
The Veth Hegemony is older than the oceans of Earth.
It has four hundred thousand worlds,

2
00:00:13,824 --> 00:00:19,558
a caste structure that has not changed in nine
hundred thousand years, and a founding

3
00:00:19,578 --> 00:00:25,110
doctrine that the human record translates,
imperfectly, as *the settled question.*

4
00:00:25,510 --> 00:00:31,349
The settled question is this: every species that
reaches the void either submits to an

5
00:00:31,369 --> 00:00:37,482
order or imposes one, and the Veth reached the void
first, and therefore the order exists,

6
00:00:37,502 --> 00:00:43,546
and therefore submission is not a defeat but an
administrative formality that has already

7
00:00:43,566 --> 00:00:46,817
taken place and merely needs to
be acknowledged.

8
00:00:47,216 --> 00:00:53,049
They have annexed eleven hundred species. They have
fought four wars in ninety thousand

9
00:00:53,069 --> 00:00:54,798
years. The wars are short.

10
00:00:55,198 --> 00:01:02,523
They arrived at Ochoa — a human colony of nine
hundred thousand people, forty-three years

11
00:01:02,543 --> 00:01:09,786
old, with a dock, two ships and a hydroponic economy
— on the fourth of April 2141, with

12
00:01:09,806 --> 00:01:13,088
thirteen vessels, and they did not fire.

13
00:01:13,608 --> 00:01:20,876
You are informed. The system is within the settled
order. Your administration continues.

14
00:01:20,896 --> 00:01:28,496
Your production is assessed at one part in nine. Your
vessels will be registered. A garrison

15
00:01:28,516 --> 00:01:31,229
will arrive in four hundred days.

16
00:01:31,631 --> 00:01:37,556
The colony's administrator — a woman of sixty-one
named Theresa Okonkwo-Vance, who had

17
00:01:37,576 --> 00:01:43,571
been elected eight months earlier on a platform
about water rights — asked the question

18
00:01:43,591 --> 00:01:49,240
that every annexed species has asked and that the
Veth have a standard answer for.

19
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:51,370
And if we decline?

20
00:01:51,771 --> 00:01:58,853
Then the system is within the settled order, your
administration does not continue, and

21
00:01:58,873 --> 00:02:02,119
a garrison arrives in four hundred days.

22
00:02:02,519 --> 00:02:08,603
She transmitted the exchange to Earth and to every
human world, in the clear, unencrypted,

23
00:02:08,623 --> 00:02:14,369
within the hour, which was not in any protocol and
which is the reason the next fifty

24
00:02:14,389 --> 00:02:16,269
years went the way they did.

25
00:02:16,669 --> 00:02:22,573
Nine hundred and eleven human settlements received
it inside four months. By the time

26
00:02:22,593 --> 00:02:28,986
it reached Earth the argument had already been running
for a third of a year on four hundred

27
00:02:29,006 --> 00:02:32,959
worlds, in public, and Albert Wesker
had not said a word.

28
00:02:33,359 --> 00:02:39,803
The narrator wants to describe the body that decided
this, because it did not exist in

29
00:02:39,823 --> 00:02:46,342
2091 and because building it is the only thing
Albert Wesker ever did that he could not

30
00:02:46,362 --> 00:02:47,168
do quickly.

31
00:02:47,568 --> 00:02:53,666
The Human Assembly had four hundred and eleven seats,
elected from the worlds by population,

32
00:02:53,686 --> 00:02:59,650
meeting on Earth and by relay. It had existed for
nineteen years. It controlled the shared

33
00:02:59,670 --> 00:03:05,369
defence budget, the Compact treaties, the drive
registry and the Progenitor protocols,

34
00:03:05,389 --> 00:03:11,420
and it had no executive at all: the Directorate
implemented what it voted, and the Hangzhou

35
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:14,478
tribunal ruled on whether the
Directorate had.

36
00:03:14,878 --> 00:03:16,215
Umbrella held no seats. Albert Wesker had a chair on
the floor, not on the benches, with

37
00:03:16,235 --> 00:03:17,695
the status of a witness who may be called and may not
vote, and he had proposed that arrangement

38
00:03:17,715 --> 00:03:19,021
himself in 2119 and the Assembly had spent four
years arguing about whether it was too

39
00:03:19,041 --> 00:03:19,807
generous or an insult before
adopting it unchanged.

40
00:03:20,207 --> 00:03:26,268
On the nineteenth of September 2141 the
Assembly called him.

41
00:03:26,788 --> 00:03:34,081
Director, the Assembly has four proposals before it.
Submit. Refuse and negotiate. Refuse

42
00:03:34,101 --> 00:03:36,218
and fight. Evacuate Ochoa.

43
00:03:36,497 --> 00:03:42,526
You are the only person alive who has fought
anything. You are also, by your own repeated

44
00:03:42,546 --> 00:03:48,370
statement, not entitled to decide this. So I am
going to ask you the only question the

45
00:03:48,390 --> 00:03:51,768
Assembly can properly ask a
witness. What is true?

46
00:03:52,717 --> 00:03:53,967
Four things.

47
00:03:54,247 --> 00:04:01,490
One. If we fight them with what we have, we lose. Not
narrowly. I have had the Red Queen

48
00:04:01,510 --> 00:04:08,671
on it since April and the model does not have an
outcome in which a human fleet engages

49
00:04:08,691 --> 00:04:15,686
a Veth battle group and anything human survives the
engagement. Anyone who tells this

50
00:04:15,706 --> 00:04:19,318
Assembly otherwise is selling
you something.

51
00:04:19,598 --> 00:04:27,208
Two. If we submit, we survive, and the terms are
genuinely one part in nine, and the Veth

52
00:04:27,228 --> 00:04:34,753
have honoured that assessment for ninety thousand
years, and eleven hundred species live

53
00:04:34,773 --> 00:04:42,383
under it and most of them are not unhappy. I want
that on the record honestly. Submission

54
00:04:42,403 --> 00:04:47,528
is not extinction. It is a tax and a
garrison and a ceiling.

55
00:04:47,807 --> 00:04:55,341
(very cold) Three. The ceiling is the point. Under
the settled order no species may hold

56
00:04:55,361 --> 00:05:02,895
a drive it did not receive from the Hegemony, may not
exceed an assessed production, and

57
00:05:02,915 --> 00:05:10,621
may not — this is the clause that matters — alter its
own biology without licence. Aeterna

58
00:05:10,641 --> 00:05:18,347
is unlicensed. The Progenitor lineage is unlicensed.
There are four hundred thousand human

59
00:05:18,367 --> 00:05:25,729
beings alive today who would be, under Veth law, a
category the translation renders as

60
00:05:25,749 --> 00:05:27,617
*unpermitted persons*.

61
00:05:28,458 --> 00:05:29,862
And the fourth thing?

62
00:05:30,262 --> 00:05:36,434
(very soft) The fourth thing is that they have made a
mistake, and I do not think anybody

63
00:05:36,454 --> 00:05:41,932
in this chamber has seen it yet, and I have been
looking at it for five months.

64
00:05:42,331 --> 00:05:48,823
The narrator asks you to notice that Albert Wesker,
at this point, had been alive in this

65
00:05:48,843 --> 00:05:55,262
world for one hundred and fifteen years, and had not
personally won anything since 2077.

66
00:05:55,781 --> 00:06:02,483
The Veth have annexed eleven hundred species. In every
case they have approached a species'

67
00:06:02,503 --> 00:06:08,835
*authority* — a throne, a council, a hierarch — and
informed it, and the authority has

68
00:06:08,855 --> 00:06:13,932
either acknowledged or been removed and
replaced with one that would.

69
00:06:14,211 --> 00:06:20,665
Their protocol has no procedure for a species that
cannot be informed, because it does

70
00:06:20,685 --> 00:06:23,902
not have a single point that
speaks for it.

71
00:06:24,182 --> 00:06:31,066
(very cold) There are four hundred and eleven worlds,
eighteen billion people, nine hundred

72
00:06:31,086 --> 00:06:37,742
settlements, four legal systems and this Assembly,
which cannot bind a colony that votes

73
00:06:37,762 --> 00:06:44,267
against it. If every one of those bodies answers the
Veth separately, at its own pace,

74
00:06:44,287 --> 00:06:51,171
in its own words, with different answers, the Hegemony
is confronted with an administrative

75
00:06:51,191 --> 00:06:55,571
condition it has not encountered in
ninety thousand years.

76
00:06:55,971 --> 00:07:00,661
You are proposing that we defeat an
interstellar empire with *paperwork*.

77
00:07:01,391 --> 00:07:08,168
Senator, I built a company that owned half this
planet's infrastructure and no government

78
00:07:08,188 --> 00:07:12,521
ever laid a finger on it, and I did
it with nothing else.

79
00:07:12,922 --> 00:07:18,373
The narrator will give you one of the four hundred
separate answers, because the campaign

80
00:07:18,393 --> 00:07:22,492
is usually described from the Assembly and
it did not happen there.

81
00:07:22,891 --> 00:07:30,079
Ochoa acknowledged the settled order in 2142,
unanimously, and Theresa Okonkwo-Vance —

82
00:07:30,099 --> 00:07:38,544
who had transmitted the Veth's demand in the clear and
started all of it — voted for acknowledgement,

83
00:07:38,564 --> 00:07:43,992
which nine hundred thousand people found
difficult to understand.

84
00:07:44,512 --> 00:07:48,950
I'll say it plainly because the recording goes out
at six. We are acknowledging. We are

85
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:52,742
not submitting; there is a difference and it
is the whole of our position.

86
00:07:53,021 --> 00:07:57,469
Their protocol requires us to acknowledge that the
system is within the settled order.

87
00:07:57,489 --> 00:08:01,937
We do acknowledge that. It is a statement about
where their maps say we are. It is not

88
00:08:01,957 --> 00:08:06,405
a statement about who we take instruction from, and
I have read all four hundred pages

89
00:08:06,425 --> 00:08:09,573
of their annexation law twice and it
does not say that it is.

90
00:08:09,853 --> 00:08:14,525
(very slow) And then we are going to file four hundred
and eleven procedural queries about

91
00:08:14,545 --> 00:08:18,955
the assessment, which their own law requires them
to answer individually, in writing,

92
00:08:18,975 --> 00:08:20,624
before a garrison may be seated.

93
00:08:21,024 --> 00:08:22,795
How long does that take them?

94
00:08:23,196 --> 00:08:28,497
Their fastest recorded response to a single query is
nine days. We have four hundred and

95
00:08:28,517 --> 00:08:32,066
eleven. And every colony that files
behind us adds its own.

96
00:08:32,905 --> 00:08:36,073
That's not a defence. That's
*filibustering an empire*.

97
00:08:36,474 --> 00:08:41,167
(very slow) Yes. We have nine hundred thousand people,
two ships and a hydroponic economy,

98
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:45,723
and the only weapon that has ever been available to
anybody in our position is that the

99
00:08:45,743 --> 00:08:49,284
people who came to take our system have
rules and we have read them.

100
00:08:49,683 --> 00:08:55,583
The Veth answered twenty-four of the four hundred and
eleven queries. The twelfth required

101
00:08:55,603 --> 00:09:01,633
them to state the basis of the assessment in a form
that Ochoa's council was able to appeal,

102
00:09:01,653 --> 00:09:07,421
and the appeal required a hearing, and there had not
been a hearing in the settled order

103
00:09:07,441 --> 00:09:08,933
in nine thousand years.

104
00:09:09,333 --> 00:09:14,423
The narrator notes that Theresa Okonkwo-Vance
had been a fisheries lawyer.

105
00:09:14,823 --> 00:09:20,612
It took seven years and it is the most-studied
campaign in human history, and not one

106
00:09:20,632 --> 00:09:22,183
human being died in it.

107
00:09:22,583 --> 00:09:29,694
Ochoa acknowledged the settled order in 2142,
unanimously, and then filed four hundred

108
00:09:29,714 --> 00:09:36,906
and eleven procedural queries about the assessment,
which the Veth protocol requires be

109
00:09:36,926 --> 00:09:41,384
answered individually before a
garrison may be seated.

110
00:09:41,783 --> 00:09:47,558
The Free Territory refused outright and invited a
garrison, which arrived and found a

111
00:09:47,578 --> 00:09:53,353
platform city of four hundred thousand that had
voted, nine days earlier, to dissolve

112
00:09:53,373 --> 00:09:59,148
its own administration, so that there was nothing
for the garrison to be seated over.

113
00:09:59,168 --> 00:10:01,193
It sat there for eleven years.

114
00:10:01,594 --> 00:10:07,690
Sixty-one colonies acknowledged. Forty refused.
Nineteen acknowledged and then seceded

115
00:10:07,710 --> 00:10:13,806
from the Assembly, which under Veth law made their
acknowledgement void and required a

116
00:10:13,826 --> 00:10:14,873
fresh approach.

117
00:10:15,272 --> 00:10:22,353
The Compact — which has no military and has never held
territory and which had spent thirty-eight

118
00:10:22,373 --> 00:10:28,942
years watching humanity with an interest that its own
historians called *unseemly* — filed

119
00:10:28,962 --> 00:10:35,458
nine hundred trade objections, every one of them
valid under a treaty the Veth had signed

120
00:10:35,478 --> 00:10:37,142
in the human year 1611.

121
00:10:37,542 --> 00:10:43,566
And the Veth admiral, whose name renders as
Sethra-Ka and who had annexed forty species

122
00:10:43,586 --> 00:10:48,081
in her career without ever raising her
voice, requested a summit.

123
00:10:48,601 --> 00:10:50,860
You are the cause of this.

124
00:10:51,261 --> 00:10:58,602
No. I proposed it. Eighteen billion people decided to
do it, in about four hundred separate

125
00:10:58,622 --> 00:11:05,640
votes, over seven years, and about a third of them
did it wrong and two colonies did it

126
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:08,552
in a way I strongly advised against.

127
00:11:08,951 --> 00:11:11,091
You are the authority.

128
00:11:11,491 --> 00:11:17,842
(very cold) Admiral, that is the assumption your
entire order rests on, and it is the

129
00:11:17,862 --> 00:11:24,213
only thing you have got wrong. I have been trying
to stop being the authority since I

130
00:11:24,233 --> 00:11:30,809
was a hundred and eleven years old. It has taken me
seventy years and it is not finished

131
00:11:30,829 --> 00:11:34,182
and it is the hardest thing I
have ever done.

132
00:11:35,131 --> 00:11:36,118
Why.

133
00:11:36,519 --> 00:11:42,891
The narrator records that the question was one word,
that the translation software rendered

134
00:11:42,911 --> 00:11:48,509
it without punctuation, and that Albert Wesker
took a long time over the answer.

135
00:11:49,029 --> 00:11:56,127
Because I was given a catalogue and no oversight when
I was young, in another world, and

136
00:11:56,147 --> 00:12:03,002
I built something magnificent out of it, and then I
did it again here, and both times

137
00:12:03,022 --> 00:12:08,339
the thing I built was perfect and nobody
in it could say no to me.

138
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:15,175
The first one ended in a volcano. This one is going
to end in an argument that will run

139
00:12:15,195 --> 00:12:22,203
for nine hundred years and that I will not win, and I
have come to prefer the second outcome,

140
00:12:22,223 --> 00:12:28,703
and it took me about sixty years to arrive at that
and I am not certain I would arrive

141
00:12:28,723 --> 00:12:29,610
there again.

142
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:34,697
The settled order has held for
ninety thousand years.

143
00:12:35,096 --> 00:12:41,697
(very cold) Yes. And in ninety thousand years it has
produced eleven hundred species that

144
00:12:41,717 --> 00:12:48,095
have never once surprised you, and one afternoon in
a system of no importance you were

145
00:12:48,115 --> 00:12:54,493
surprised by a hydroponic colony with two ships. I
would ask you to consider what that

146
00:12:54,513 --> 00:13:00,965
is worth, because it is the only thing in this room
that neither of us can manufacture.

147
00:13:01,365 --> 00:13:08,276
The Hegemony withdrew from the Ochoa system in 2151
under an instrument it insisted on

148
00:13:08,296 --> 00:13:15,287
calling a *deferral of assessment*, and which every
species in nine hundred light years

149
00:13:15,307 --> 00:13:16,495
read correctly.

150
00:13:16,895 --> 00:13:22,841
It is the only recorded case of a Veth withdrawal
without combat in ninety thousand years,

151
00:13:22,861 --> 00:13:28,541
and the Veth have never permitted it to be called
anything else, and the Compact has a

152
00:13:28,561 --> 00:13:32,916
word for it that the human record renders
as *the long polite no*.
